# CLAIRITY environment variables
#
# The app talks to Claude through the Cloudflare Worker in ../server, which holds
# the Anthropic key server-side. See server/README.md.
#
# WHERE TO SET THESE:
#   - Local build: copy this file to `.env` (which is gitignored).
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* values are compiled into the app bundle and can be extracted from
# the binary. That is why the Anthropic key is no longer among them. The client
# token below ships too — it is a doorkeeper, not a secret. It is worth having
# because it can be rotated with one `wrangler secret put`, takes effect
# immediately, and is useless anywhere except this proxy.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE=https://clairity-api.clairity.workers.dev
EXPO_PUBLIC_CLIENT_TOKEN=

# Direct-to-Anthropic fallback, for local development only.
#
# With EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE set above, this is ignored. Setting it INSTEAD of the
# proxy puts a billable key inside the app bundle, so never do that in a build
# that leaves your machine — not TestFlight, and certainly not the App Store.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
